From steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:51:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd: start capture asynchronously and drain playback outside the lock

PCM_START for a capture stream ran stop/configure/initialize/start_unit on the
control-queue thread while holding the shared `hosts` mutex, which the pump
thread takes every iteration. Opening the microphone (permission prompt,
device selection) can take over a second, and the guest's control-message
timeout is 1 s, so the message timed out, PipeWire was SIGKILLed and games
froze. START now replies immediately and a worker thread builds, configures and
starts the input unit; no AudioUnit call runs under the `hosts` mutex (capture's
stop_unit takes the unit out under the `capture` mutex, and the stop runs after
that lock is released). A start also leaves the stop of an already-running unit
to that worker (see `stop_pending`), so `AudioOutputUnitStop` cannot block under
`hosts` either. Until the unit runs, capture I/O is completed with silence so
the guest stream keeps flowing; a failed start logs once and keeps delivering
silence. Playback behaviour is unchanged.

release() also polled the playback drain (play_out) up to MAX_BUFFER_MS+100 ms
while holding `hosts`. The wait is now bounded by the ring's consumed pointer
and runs after the lock is released, so a slow drain cannot stall the pump
thread and, with it, every other stream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
